  {
   "key": "0x06",
   "name": "noise period",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
     "lines": "650-682"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "function": "ay8910_device::ay8910_write_reg",
     "case": [
      "AY_NOISEPER"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "R6 is the noise period register: its lower 5 bits, B4 to B0, are the 5-bit noise period.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "654-656",
       "sha": "9a6be09f12a5d9cfb98d60dfa6e4510cfb2f3ee52fd61ca3aa3faa5010882af1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Writing R6 sets the noise period from bits B4 to B0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "654-656",
       "sha": "9a6be09f12a5d9cfb98d60dfa6e4510cfb2f3ee52fd61ca3aa3faa5010882af1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The noise generator counts the input clock down by 16 and then down by the programmed 5-bit noise period.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "652-654",
       "sha": "fdf0b5644fa7a932ae2b59308ad3b15cebb747868d59b9b8ac42c82d5b895441"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The noise period is a period: the higher the value, the lower the noise frequency.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "663-664",
       "sha": "6928f1aeaf869a300dd3e6d2a72a51353e4160c7546ec05375b8855d01fbe40d"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The lowest noise period is 00001, which divides by 1, and the highest is 11111, which divides by 31.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "665-666",
       "sha": "7b6792064b65d5e14cd7fa12e2c5048f3b7ecf51cc4e17359f538ec422ccc609"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The document gives the equation from the input clock and the noise period to the noise frequency.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "667-673",
       "sha": "72961c9345c93200433e9a3c87ac38704352c1c3574021afd5169110318965db"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "With a 2 MHz input clock the noise frequencies range from 4 kHz to 125 kHz.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "674-678",
       "sha": "ff17dfbce49ece64808345e9a7676427ef5474b3092e7ee5079ffb213f42fdb1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The document rearranges the noise equation to give the noise period register value from the clock and the wanted frequency.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "679-681",
       "sha": "ac2a3bdf1f987bd5e077047d739d0295a382a26b1f854166ff9951fb45496e7c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "9",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "On the AY8930 in expanded mode the noise period keeps all 8 bits of R6, where the AY-3-8910 keeps 5.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.h",
       "lines": "283",
       "sha": "4a5a897c68813f4338e0a8b3bd507560d3c6b8ec3ba2e17a3abe836187501692"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
