  {
   "key": "0x07",
   "name": "mixer and port direction",
   "aliases": [
    "enable"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
     "lines": "683-720"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "function": "ay8910_device::ay8910_write_reg",
     "case": [
      "AY_ENABLE"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "R7 is a multi-function enable register that controls the three noise and tone mixers and the two general purpose I/O ports.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "686-687",
       "sha": "ed4a9aa5745931ac94c04a3a1dabde61467641746ff66512c65c81dbf15d857a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bits B5 to B0 of R7 pick, per channel, whether noise, tone, both or neither are combined; a 0 enables.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "688-691",
       "sha": "7647be63fff9754362b8827a400f9c3df9db2d0c419e93eab89d78d53a44444d"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "698-704",
       "sha": "62582c1fd7b3803fa133f9e1701ff5aa313ecdf338a7181195f61fd1c9ba3f28"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "705-710",
       "sha": "423982eb787b92a0117955a4372b07d6746312809a6b5644425fc00e2c2639c8"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A write to R7 sets, in bits B7 and B6, the direction of I/O ports B and A: 1 is output and 0 is input.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "692-694",
       "sha": "c4c4909562b23a75cfb55f08a74b301462f1799cd6b5b81d5879b073d2159c91"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "711-717",
       "sha": "db2ae4f12cbecfe5df5f1255ae1962c2a7a81848687939e230b9c4388a709f4c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Disabling noise and tone does not turn a channel off; only zero in its amplitude register does.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "718-720",
       "sha": "7280fadf0be659fec79d9876773e5b8ca076b75c67e867e5365468e1f1133a87"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
