  {
   "key": "0x08..0x0A",
   "name": "channel amplitude",
   "aliases": [
    "volume"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
     "lines": "721-793"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "function": "ay8910_device::ay8910_write_reg",
     "case": [
      "AY_AVOL"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "function": "ay8910_device::ay8910_write_reg",
     "case": [
      "AY_BVOL"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "function": "ay8910_device::ay8910_write_reg",
     "case": [
      "AY_CVOL"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "R10, R11 and R12 are the amplitude registers of channels A, B and C; the lower 5 bits, B4 to B0, determine the amplitude.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "721-724",
       "sha": "e2df33b806498db0956f4b26f86f3b7a871ca7e0536049040ce0ee964251f4d2"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "725-729",
       "sha": "f425d739d9cbea52999ecf761451664e13dd5aae23024439b4cf7144ab36f272"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A write to an amplitude register sets, in bits L3 to L0, the fixed amplitude level, which counts only when M is 0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "736-743",
       "sha": "7e9f742bd805fee19e5163b9d5d157a13ffd87c74f1274554565631152996446"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A write to an amplitude register sets the mode bit M: 0 selects a fixed level amplitude and 1 the envelope generator's output.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "734-735",
       "sha": "74e77cb33b0ad3723fe17eb77eea48322a91712eee434a84b2f3f9032cd1181f"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "744-750",
       "sha": "5fe4de320986c7ccdff2381273aa2d2f071987b3326d9c7ad3d4d9917279e86b"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A fixed level amplitude is one of the 16 levels, set by the decimal value of bits L3 to L0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "780-784",
       "sha": "f49bdc47518767c3341478645d4a68dc28064694df801e7520c8a72b91f32163"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "In expanded mode the AY8930 keeps a 5-bit fixed level and takes the mode from bit 5; a chip with extended envelope has a 2-bit mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.h",
       "lines": "277-278",
       "sha": "108ac353d7111b8c06dc658d184adb8189f6aa4fd07436e3ee047ca6d9a494f4"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
