  {
   "key": "0x0B..0x0C",
   "name": "envelope period",
   "aliases": [],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
     "lines": "794-852"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "function": "ay8910_device::ay8910_write_reg",
     "case": [
      "AY_EACOARSE"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "R13 and R14 set the frequency of the envelope, and R15 sets its shape and cycle pattern.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "799-803",
       "sha": "829752fcdd9a1bf4a842658257ae93109e36b92295cf70803abfc58f0e377b58"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The 16-bit envelope period is the coarse tune register R14 as EP15 to EP8 over the fine tune register R13 as EP7 to EP0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "809-813",
       "sha": "8fff9b2e47907735b6a56b155021f79394a7cf5669ab79549115006fbe778759"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "828-831",
       "sha": "3e7f0ea2f298d7406b6329721ed951bad640531058a89c34554b5f0371b69f92"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The envelope generator counts the input clock down by 256 and then down by the programmed 16-bit envelope period.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "807-809",
       "sha": "0c10dd6a9176b6958f431825a680eb23373ec7a2fc4cac3a86ecbe29e5888667"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The envelope period is a period: the higher the value, the lower the envelope frequency.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "814-816",
       "sha": "ec990a3fabb65a6cb5f1ed419bc0b17f0b3ff665125cb3f5d21ca9643b1c8a92"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The lowest envelope period is 1, which divides by 1, and the highest is 65535.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "817-819",
       "sha": "6ee5fe509447ec852191a3cabb56419ed7359c65729f057bb7bd283ccd73f4fe"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The document gives the equation from the input clock and the envelope period to the envelope frequency.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "820-827",
       "sha": "6565e6ab69f3b07ccdeeeff6bfccdd5b3a2e1cd3688b96122560720abdb2c0c2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "With a 2 MHz clock the envelope frequencies range from 0.12 Hz to 7812.5 Hz.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "832-835",
       "sha": "733f98d94d98126fc6e455c5798fcabfda97fe199adf6de9ab7adbb8b352e684"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The document rearranges the envelope equation to give the period registers from the clock and the wanted frequency.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "835-840",
       "sha": "e605dd17d41fc84b8b72bb500e6d99d86d9371d393902b2e510f46b710686d5f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "9",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "From a 2 MHz clock, a 0.5 Hz envelope has coarse tune 00111101 and fine tune 00001001.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "841-852",
       "sha": "74f502aecb665d4e690801bc832c4f2640324b4e22b1f6c5b06c3fbcdcfe3a4c"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
     "lines": "794-798",
     "as": "key"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
     "lines": "804-806",
     "as": "see-also"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "lines": "925",
     "as": "decode"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "lines": "955-956",
     "as": "agrees",
     "row": "2"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "key": "0x0D",
   "name": "envelope shape",
   "aliases": [
    "shape"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
     "lines": "853-929"
    },
    {
     "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
     "function": "ay8910_device::ay8910_write_reg",
     "case": [
      "AY_EASHAPE"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The envelope generator counts the envelope frequency down by 16, giving a 16-state envelope pattern on its 4-bit output E3 to E0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "854-859",
       "sha": "946552f25fc30a32c014b280d8b7faa68fe062a2f65cd14395f7adfd260f5c8f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "A write to R15 sets, in its lower 4 bits B3 to B0, the envelope shape and cycle control, each bit controlling one function.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "860-862",
       "sha": "06ca8edec4de20a8af340fe8eb5ee1988b3b7517b99ca2e30eeafd9daa28b6aa"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Hold set to 1 limits the envelope to one cycle, holding the last count, 0000 or 1111 by direction.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "883-887",
       "sha": "1a75229273932b41542048e7345b792a83b98c4ea092b817af0fd182f1fb5bd5"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Alternate set to 1 makes the envelope counter reverse its count direction after each cycle.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "888-889",
       "sha": "e0847b03b0c2d32b20f5f8d128f8a6805aef4e2d0f489b977557da34dfae729b"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "With both Hold and Alternate set to 1 the envelope counter is reset to its initial count before holding.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "890-891",
       "sha": "8342940857b28795b42f62af16e907462f3961d8e90508132b3f40487aa9b222"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Attack set to 1 counts the envelope up from 0000 to 1111; set to 0 it counts down from 1111 to 0000.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "896-899",
       "sha": "6d0c7d3b7b57ed86e81f6f0907f42aa8204ab8c318b90a11d20f2e4192655f77"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Continue set to 1 gives the cycle pattern the Hold bit defines; set to 0 the envelope resets to 0000 after one cycle and holds.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:AY-3-8910.raw.txt",
       "lines": "900-905",
       "sha": "3afa0b439a02f5cf6e2ed5fce8a5e5bd26eedd71a10dd3c987e44b0664b7a0b3"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "mame",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "On the AY8930 a write to R15 keeps a mode in bits 7 to 4, and entering or leaving expanded mode clears registers 0x00 to 0x0C and 0x10 to 0x1C.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
       "lines": "975-986",
       "sha": "a429c70689cfb7f75c8f65e30a94df1c3dd2273d66375656b1ba4aab642e0211"
      },
      {
       "ref": "mame:src/devices/sound/ay8910.cpp",
       "lines": "987-992",
       "sha": "99c21a056c9c3e5d71adac0ce70bafcd77c01016aae42d47704dfeccf6da8061"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
